@startuml platform_probe
!theme plain
title Platform Driver Probe Flow

participant DTParser as "Device Tree\nParser"
participant PlatformBus as "Platform\nBus Core"
participant DriverCore as "Driver\nManager"
participant Driver
participant Hardware

== Device Discovery ==
DTParser -> PlatformBus: Register platform_device\n(from DTS node)
note right of DTParser
  Creates platform_device for each
  compatible DTS node
  Sets pdev->dev.of_node
end note

== Driver Matching ==
PlatformBus -> DriverCore: New device registered
DriverCore -> DriverCore: Iterate registered drivers
DriverCore -> Driver: Check of_device_id match\n(compatible string)

alt No match found
  DriverCore -> PlatformBus: Device unbound
  note right of DriverCore
    Device waits for matching driver
    (can load later via modprobe)
  end note
else Match found
  DriverCore -> Driver: Call probe()
end

== Probe Execution ==
activate Driver
Driver -> Driver: struct my_dev *dev =\ndevm_kzalloc()

Driver -> Driver: Get memory resource\n(platform_get_resource)
Driver -> Driver: ioremap_resource()
Driver -> Driver: Read DTS properties\n(of_property_read_*)

Driver -> Driver: Request IRQ\n(devm_request_irq)

Driver -> Driver: Initialize hardware\nWrite control registers

Driver -> Driver: Register subsystem\n(gpiochip_add, etc)
Driver -> Driver: Create sysfs files

Driver -> Hardware: Hardware ready
Driver --> DriverCore: return 0 (success)
deactivate Driver

DriverCore -> PlatformBus: Probe complete

note right of Driver
  devm_* functions auto-cleanup
  on probe failure or device removal

  If probe fails:
  - Return -errno
  - Kernel frees all devm resources
  - Device remains unbound
end note

@enduml
